  "explanation": "Zero query and key weights give uniform attention over all 11 positions at '='. Only token '1' contributes a value, scaled by 11, so coordinate 1 becomes the number n of ones. The ten hidden units compute ReLU(n-j) for j=0,...,9. Their weighted sum in coordinate 2 is -1+2ReLU(n)+4 sum_{j=1}^9 (-1)^j ReLU(n-j), which equals -1 for even n and +1 for odd n. Opposite readout weights select the correct bit; '=' and '_' have logits -2. All omitted weights remain zero.",
